7.  BOTH FOOTINGS ON EVERY CONCLUSION OF THIS AUDIT, AND A SECOND MUTATION CONTROL
==============================================================================================================================
    footing        median  rich N>=10  poor N<10  rho(N,boost)        p  sep from 2.11
    canonical       0.817       1.431      0.604        +0.330   0.1026         +0.412
    alt             0.746       1.307      0.551        +0.330   0.1004         +0.452
  [PASS] F1 both footings give the same audit verdict on the richness confound   (canonical rho +0.330 p 0.1026; alt rho +0.330 p 0.1004)
  [PASS] F2 MUTATION CONTROL -- shuffle the measured dispersions across groups.  The N-trend must be destroyed, because it is a pairing between a group's own richness and its own kinematics.  If it survived a shuffle it would be an artefact of the baryon budget or the radii, not of the dispersions   (shuffled rho(N, log boost) = -0.059 +- 0.179; real +0.330)

==============================================================================================================================
8.  VERDICT OF THE AUDIT
==============================================================================================================================
    * The arithmetic REPRODUCES: median boost 0.817 canonical / 0.746 alt, bootstrap [0.656, 1.110].
    * The 'consistent with unity, cannot discriminate' half of the claim STANDS and is if anything
      understated -- see D1.
    * The '3.6 sigma from the cluster rows' half does NOT stand at that strength: 3.6 sigma
      statistical-only becomes 2.3 sigma once the file's OWN admissible systematic bracket is
      included, and that still counts nothing on the cluster side.
    * Richness confound: rho(N, log boost) = +0.330, permutation p = 0.1026 -- NOT significant, and
      said so: check A1 PASSES.  What is established is not a trend but a FRAGILITY.  The N >= 10 groups sit
      at 1.43 and the N < 10 groups at 0.60; a quality cut any referee would ask for moves the
      rung onto the liability table's mildest X-ray rows (1.45, 1.48), separation +0.006 dex (E2).
    * Unmodelled per-group scatter 0.310 dex against a quoted statistical 0.276 dex; chi^2/dof = 3.15, so the 26
      groups are NOT draws from one value and the bootstrap band is not the whole error.
    * LambdaCDM, zero free parameters, lands at 0.61 on the same groups with the same pipeline -- it
      does not show the cluster deficit either.  So the group/cluster contrast does not isolate 'counted vs
      modelled baryons'; it is equally a statement about galaxy-kinematic vs X-ray-hydrostatic estimators.

